## Lunar repositories

- In repositories under `~/code/lunar`, run tests directly rather than through `shuttle run test`.
- If tests need local infrastructure, use `shuttle run local_up`. If they need environment variables, use `shuttle run generate_dotenv`.
- When investigating another Lunar repository, prefer an existing local clone and update it with `jj`; otherwise clone it or use the organization Sourcegraph instance via `src`.
{{- end }}

## Code changes

- Write comments that explain why rather than restating what the code does.
- After changing code, run the relevant formatter, linter, type checker, and tests. If suitable tooling is unavailable, say so.
- Use the project-local `tmp` directory for temporary artifacts; it is globally ignored by VCS. Put resumable notes in `tmp/notes` and prefix their filenames with `YYYY-MM-DD`.
- Never commit production data. Anonymize any PII retained in tests, comments, or commit descriptions.

## GitHub

- Do not push commits or bookmarks or publish comments, reviews, or replies without an explicit request for that specific external action.
- Prefer `gh` over fetching GitHub web pages directly. When already in the relevant repository, prefer local history over the GitHub API.
